# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. First, because this package reads an API key from the environment.
#
# .Rprofile is here because the README documents it as a place to put
# OPENAI_API_KEY. A project .Rprofile is otherwise a perfectly normal thing to
# commit, so if you use one for settings rather than secrets, keep the key in
# .Renviron and un-ignore this line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Renviron
.Rprofile
.Rprofile.local
.env
*.pem
.httr-oauth
.secrets

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R build and check output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.Rcheck/
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.Rout
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj
src/*.o
src/*.so
src/*.dll

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
*~
\#*\#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Package runtime output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gptread.log
gptread_history_*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One-time migration scaffolding. These exist to get from the previous release
# to this one; they are not part of the package and do not belong in history.
# Delete them once the migration commit is in.
#
# Note `run-tests.sh` and `.github/` are deliberately NOT here -- they are
# ongoing development tooling and should be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
REVIEW.md
COMMIT_MSG.txt
migrate.sh
_old_gptread/
legacy_v1/_scratch/
